Trust this connection's own just-committed refs in chunkStoreForceRefresh.

chunkStoreForceRefresh's fast path (csDiskStateMatchesMemory) proves the
on-disk store still matches memory by stat-ing the file and reading its tail
root record through the chunk store's own long-lived file handle. On native
VFSes a write made through that handle is immediately visible to a stat on
the same handle, so the fast path reliably fires right after this
connection's own commit.

Emscripten's DriveFS (used by the wasm build to share a filesystem across
worker threads) does not have that property: writes are buffered on the open
stream and only pushed back to the backing store when the stream is closed,
but stat/getattr calls are served from the backing store regardless of any
still-open writer. So on wasm, csDiskStateMatchesMemory's stat-based check
reports a same-connection commit as stale even though nothing actually
changed, which sends chunkStoreForceRefresh down the reload path. Right
after `dolt_clone`, that reload replaces the in-memory refs table with a
fresh (but, per the DriveFS quirk above, momentarily still-stale) view that
is missing the `origin` remote `dolt_clone` itself just added, so the very
next statement -- `dolt_remote('set-url', 'origin', ...)`, run by
rusqdoltlite to restore the canonical clone URL -- fails with
SQLITE_NOTFOUND ("remote not found").

Add a one-shot ChunkStore::bTrustLocalAfterCommit flag: chunkStoreCommit
sets it after a successful on-disk commit, and chunkStoreForceRefresh's fast
path treats it as equivalent to csDiskStateMatchesMemory returning true,
clearing it either way once consumed. This only ever short-circuits the very
next force-refresh immediately following this connection's own commit; any
later reload (uncommitted local writes, or a fast-path miss for any other
reason) still goes through the normal disk-verified path unchanged.

diff --git a/doltlite.c b/doltlite.c
index 360f935..1bcacc3 100644
--- a/doltlite.c
+++ b/doltlite.c
@@ -23646,6 +23646,18 @@ struct ChunkStore {
 
   /* Prevent checkpoint reentry through VFS write hooks. */
   int checkpointActive;
+
+  /* Set right after this connection's own chunkStoreCommit persists refs to
+  ** disk; consumed (cleared) by the very next chunkStoreForceRefresh call.
+  ** Some VFS backends (notably Emscripten's DriveFS, used by the wasm build)
+  ** only make a written file's stat/size visible to callers after the
+  ** writing stream is closed, so csDiskStateMatchesMemory's disk probe can
+  ** report a same-connection commit as stale even though nothing changed.
+  ** This flag lets the immediate post-commit refresh trust the state it
+  ** just wrote instead of tripping the reload path, avoiding a spurious
+  ** "remote not found" warning from statements like dolt_remote('set-url')
+  ** that immediately follow a clone/pull on the same connection. */
+  u8 bTrustLocalAfterCommit;
 };
 
 void csManifestSeal(u8 *aBuf);
@@ -97405,6 +97417,18 @@ struct ChunkStore {
 
   /* Prevent checkpoint reentry through VFS write hooks. */
   int checkpointActive;
+
+  /* Set right after this connection's own chunkStoreCommit persists refs to
+  ** disk; consumed (cleared) by the very next chunkStoreForceRefresh call.
+  ** Some VFS backends (notably Emscripten's DriveFS, used by the wasm build)
+  ** only make a written file's stat/size visible to callers after the
+  ** writing stream is closed, so csDiskStateMatchesMemory's disk probe can
+  ** report a same-connection commit as stale even though nothing changed.
+  ** This flag lets the immediate post-commit refresh trust the state it
